A||N||7||contra||Antenna Mod||||10||
Z||000000||contra||07-27-2000||06:58 PM||||I am prepping my car for paint right now, sanding all the bondo on all the chips, and smoothing out all the bondo on the scoops and lowering dam i put on the car as well. Well as i was looking at the car, i thought to myself, "Damn i hate that big a s s antenna."<BR>So i unscrewed it, slipped a medium thickness wire under the fender and wrapped it onto the screw where the antenna usually screws onto. Then i put a nut on it, and bondo'd it all in. I took the rest of the wire and wrapped it around my trunk space (up front of course), and closed the front hood.<BR>Works just as good as before, except now i dont have that annoying long antenna. i think the fiero looks better with no antenna. i'll post pictures as soon as my car gets painted this weekend  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||10
Z||000001||286SE'S||07-27-2000||07:09 PM||||Nice Idea. Makes putting the car cover on al ot easier. I used to unscrew the antenna to put the cover on, then lost the antenna cause it was loose. Then cut a hole in the cover for it. <BR>Terry<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||DaRkLoRD||07-27-2000||08:06 PM||||Cool mod!!<P>what kind of wire did you use? and what length?<P>I can't wait to see pics of your car, it sounds like it's gonna be awesome..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A> <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||10
Z||000003||Phantom Rage||07-27-2000||09:09 PM||||I think you can still get the (inside) window tape mounted antennas.  I believe Radio Shack might still carry them.  The antenna is thin and flexible, kind of like thin speaker wire. You plug it into the radio's antenna input, with the factory one removed, then stick the antenna to the inside glass with it's pre packaged tape. I can't remember but I think the tape is already stuck to the antenna. Hide it by sticking it, as close to the a-pillar's and headliner, as you can. <P><BR>I've seen plugs on some older VW's, pre-Futaba’s ones. They cover up the hole with the antenna removed.   The plugs sometimes sport the car make, model, or manufactures symbol.  The one’s I saw were rectangle in shape but had rounded edges and contoured to the cars body.   <BR>||||reg||7
Z||000004||contra||07-27-2000||09:28 PM||||yeah exactly<BR>i used a wire similar to speaker wire<BR>i'm doing some research on antennas to see if i can amplify the signal a bit more. i'm guessing at either by coiling it, or adding some low current electricity to it...but i'll save that topic until i know the real answer  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> for now it works great.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Robert||07-27-2000||10:12 PM||||We I first put on my car cover; I removed the antenna, to cut the hole in the cover.  <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/carcover.jpg"> <P>I liked the look of the car without the antenna so much; I went out and bought an aftermarket window antenna with a 12-volt booster at PepBoys ($14.00).  It sits under the dash, and works just fine.  I then took a cap from a BIC pen, cut it down a little and put it where the antenna was.  To me it looks like I have a power antenna, in the down position.  What do you guys think?<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/antenna.jpg"> <P><P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://canterburytrails.com/photo/T2.GIF"> ||||reg||10
Z||000006||86SE||07-28-2000||01:06 AM||||After painting my car, I was puttin the panels back on, went to screw in the antenna.........its not ment to turn more than 1/4 of a turn after you think its tight enough, i found out the hard way....  Twisted right off!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  Welded it back on, started the plastic surround on fire, blew the fire out, but JB weld in its place, and its still kinda tilted to the right.....<P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero||||reg||1
Z||000007||Monkeyman||07-28-2000||02:04 AM||||I have a fake cell phone window mount antenna for my CB (on the rear window).  I'll probably find another to use for the stereo.  Just one looks weird.||||reg||1
